Let $p$ be a real number such that $1 < p \le 2$ and consider the operator $T_g$ defined through the integral formula \begin{align*}
T_g(f)(z) &= \int_{\mathbb{D}} \frac{1-|w|^2}{|w-z|^2}P_{p-1}\left(\frac{z+w}{zw}\right)g(w)\,dw.
\end{align*} This operator $T_g$ is compact from $BMOA_p$ to $BMOA_1$ when $p > 2$ is established in \cite{Liu2019}. Our main findings include: \begin{itemize} \item The operator $T_g$ is weakly compact from $BMOA_p$ to $BMOA_p$ for $1 < p \le 2$. \item The operator $T_g$ is compact from $BMOA_p$ to $BMOA_1$ for $1 < p \le 2$. \end{itemize}
